    "pinyin": "zhèyīdiǎn wǒ zhàn shūshu zhèbian. sānfútiān chuī kōngtiáo, hánqì jìn le shēntǐ, dōngtiān jiù yào shēngbìng. suǒyǐ wǒ měi nián rùfú dōu tiē sānfútiē, dōngbìngxiàzhì ma.",
    "en": "I'm with him on that. Air conditioning in the dog days lets the cold into your body, and then you fall ill in winter. That's why I put on the dog-day plasters every summer: treat winter illness in the summer."
